From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ville Takio <ville+git@takio.fi>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 12:46:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: b43: N-PHY: RX I/Q calibration for rev 3 and later

b43_nphy_rev3_cal_rx_iq() is a stub returning -1, so N-PHY rev 3 and up
never get RX I/Q compensation: the C1/C2_RXIQ_COMPA0/B0/A1/B1 registers
(0x09a-0x09d) stay 0. On a BCM43217 (N-PHY rev 17, radio 2057 rev 14,
external PA) writing the vendor driver's values into them by hand takes
TCP upload from about 57 to 71 Mbit/s.

With this calibration, on that board (RT-AC56U, HT20 ch1, a two-stream
phone at -37 dBm, iperf3 TCP -P4, alternating with the module without
it): upload 38.0 and 57.3 Mbit/s without, 76.9 and 77.9 with, the phone
sending at MCS 15 instead of MCS 13; download unchanged (72.1/82.4 and
81.9/80.5). The coefficients it finds are of the vendor's sign and size
(0x004f 0x03fb 0x0029 0x03f9 against 0x006a 0x03ff 0x0034 0).

Port the calibration from brcmsmac's wlc_phy_cal_rxiq_nphy_rev3(), with
its helpers: the PHY and radio setup and cleanup for the loopback, the RX
gain control for the tone, the TX power index setting it uses, and the RC
sweep of the RX LPF that the full calibration runs on rev 3-6 (radio
2056). Both the rev 3-6 and the rev 7+ (radio 2057) branches are ported.

Fixes this needs in existing code:
- b43_nphy_calc_rx_iq_comp() worked the coefficients out in u16 and had
  the sign of the rounding term wrong, so it could not produce valid
  values. Port brcmsmac's wlc_phy_calc_rx_iq_comp_nphy() instead, with
  its 32-bit arithmetic. As there, a failed estimate is measured twice
  more but the old coefficients are kept. Rev 2 shares this function;
  its calibration is still not reached at init.
- The rev 7 RF control override table had the wrong value masks for
  fields 0x0100 and 0x0200 of override 1 (bits 8 and 9 instead of 11 and
  12). Nothing used them until now.
- b43_nphy_run_samples() entered the carrier search unconditionally.
  That resets the CCA and forces the RF sequence to RX, undoing the
  RX2TX loopback set up for the calibration. As in brcmsmac, do it only
  with hang avoidance (N-PHY rev 3 and 4), and leave the carrier search
  before the samples start.
- Keep the TX gain table's gm value (gmval), which the RX gain control
  uses at 5 GHz, and start with no fixed TX power index set.

b43 never reached the calibration at init: perical is 2 (multi-phase, as
wl) and the multi-phase calibration is not implemented. Until it is, run
its RX I/Q step at init on rev 3-18, as brcmsmac's RXCAL phase does, and
save the calibration when it succeeds. The TX I/Q and LO calibration
stays off.

Signed-off-by: Ville Takio <ville+git@takio.fi>
---
